\par }\pard\plain \s1\qc \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin720\lin720\itap0 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\ul\insrsid12192131 CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\f0\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard\plain \s1\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin720\lin720\itap0 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\ul\insrsid12192131 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 We are pleased to offer you, the position of \'93}{\fs21\insrsid9321002  CCE}{\fs21\insrsid12192131  }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131  }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 \'94 with }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 NRI Business Solutions Pvt. Ltd}{
\fs21\insrsid12192131 . (hereinafter referred to as the \lquote }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 NRIBS}{\fs21\insrsid12192131 \rquote ) on the following terms and conditions:
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 1.   Commencement of employment
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx0\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 1.1 Your employment will be effective, as of}{\fs21\insrsid12192131  12}{\fs21\super\insrsid12192131\charrsid12192131 th}{\fs21\insrsid12192131  Dec. 2005}{
\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par 1.2\tab The employee agrees and understands that he/she shall be bound by the general terms and conditions of employment whic
h is annexed hereto and marked as Schedule III. The employee further understands that he/she be bound by the amendments made to the general terms and conditions of employment from time to time by the NRIBS.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 2.  Job title
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par Your job title will be \'93}{\fs21\insrsid8794687 Customer Care Executive}{\fs21\insrsid12192131 \'94.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 3}{\fs21\insrsid12192131 .  Your salary and other benefits will be as set out in Schedule 1, here to.
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\b\f1\fs21 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.\tab}}\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec\pnf1\pnstart4\pnindent360 {\pntxta .}}\faauto\ls1\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 
NRIBS  property
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 4.1}{\fs21\insrsid12192131  The employee herein shall always maintain in good condition NRIBS property, which may be entrusted to you for official use during the cou
rse of your employment and return all such property to the NRIBS prior to relinquishment of your charge, failing which the cost of the same will be recovered from you by the NRIBS.
\par 
\par 4.2\tab The employee herein shall always disclose and assign to the NRIBS as the NRIBS\rquote 
s exclusive property, free from any obligations to the employee, all copyrightable works, inventions and technical or business innovations developed or conceived by the employee solely or jointly with others during the period of the employee\rquote s emp
loyment,(1) that are along the lines of the business, work or investigations of the NRIBS or its affiliates to which his/her employment relates or as to which the employee may receive information due to his/her employment, or (2) that result from or are s
u
ggested by any work which the employee may do for the NRIBS or (3) that are otherwise made through the use NRIBS time, facilities or materials. The employee further shall make and maintain for the NRIBS adequate and current written records as to the above
 mentioned.
\par 
\par 4.3 The employee shall execute all necessary papers and otherwise provide proper assistance, during and subsequent to his/her employment to enable the NRIBS to obtain from itself or its nominees, patents, copyrights or other  legal protection f
or such copyrightable works, inventions or innovations in any and all countries.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx0\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
4.4 The employee will not disclose or utilize in his/her work with the NRIBS any secret or Confidential information of others (including any prior employers), or any inventio
ns or innovations of the employee which are not included within the scope of this Agreement.
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx360\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 5. Termination
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par The NRIBS and employee acknowledge that Employee\rquote s employment hereunder is and shall continue to be at will, and may be terminated at any time, with or without cause, at the option of the NRIBS. If Employee\rquote 
s employment terminates for any reasons, Employee shall not be entitled to any payments, benefits,
 damages, awards or compensation other than as specifically provided by this Agreement, or as may otherwise be available pursuant to other written agreements entered into by and between the NRIBS and the employee. No provision of this Agreement shall be c
onstrued as conferring upon Employee a right to continue as an employee of the NRIBS.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par 5.1\tab The employee may terminate his/her employment with the NRIBS, by giving no less than one month\rquote s prior notice or salary for unsaved period, if any, left after adjustment of pending leaves, as on date.
\par 
\par 5.2\tab The NRIBS reserve the right to terminate the employee\rquote s employment summarily without any notice period or termination payment, if it has reasonable ground to believe that the employee is guilty of misconduct or negli
gence, or have committed any fundamental breach of this contract or caused any loss to the NRIBS.
\par 
\par 5.3\tab Any employee knowingly or intentionally conceals, destroys or alerts or intentionally or knowingly causes another to conceal, destroys or alerts any comp
uter source code used for a computer program, computer system or computer network, when the computer source code is required to be kept or maintained by the NRIBS shall be terminated by the NRIBS without giving any prior notice to the employee.
\par 
\par 5.4\tab If the employee without permission of the owner or any other person who is in charge of  a computer, computer system or computer network:-
\par 
\par a).Accesses or secures access to such computer, computer system or computer network;
\par 
\par b) downloads copies or extracts any data, computer data base or information from such computer, computer system or computer network including information or data held or stored in any removable storage medium;
\par 
\par c) introduce or causes to be introduced any computer contaminant or computer virus into any computer, computer system or computer network;
\par 
\par d) damages or causes to be damages any computer, computer system or computer network, data, computer data base or any other programmes residing in such computer, computer system or computer network;
\par 
\par f) Denies, causes the denial of access to any person authorized to access any compute, computer system or computer network by any means;
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx540\tx1440\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 g) provides any assistance to any person to facilitate access to a computer, computer system or computer network in
 contravention of the provisions of this Act, rules or regulations made there under;
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par h. charges the services availed of by a person to the account 
of another person by tampering with or manipulating any computer system, or computer network, he/she be liable to be terminated by the NRIBS without giving any notice in writing and/or that employee shall be liable for a fine, for any amount which shall b
e the discretion of the NRIBS.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 5.5 On the termination of the employee\rquote s employment for whatever reason, the employee shall return to the NRIBS all property; documents and papers, both original and copies thereof, including any samples, literature, contr
acts, records, list, drawings, blueprints, letters, notes, data and the like and Confidential information in your possession or under your control relating to your employment or to clients\rquote  business affairs.
\par 
\par 5.6 The employee further understands that the t
erms of this contract of employment shall be for a period of not less than six months proceeding the date of execution of this contract. The NRIBS reserves its right to renew this contract with the employee from time to time with the NRIBS if deemed fit.

\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 6. Confidential information
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par During the employment with the NRIBS the employee will devote whole time, attention and skill to the best of the employee\rquote s ability for the NRIBS\rquote s business. The employee shall not, directly or indirectly engage or associate hi
mself with, be connected with, concerned, employed or engaged in any other business or activities or any other post or work part time or pursue any course of study whatsoever, without the prior permission of the NRIBS.
\par 
\par 6.1 The employee shall always mainta
in the highest degree of confidentially and keep as confidential the records, documents and other Confidential Information relating to the business of NRIBS which may be known to him/her or confided in him/her by any means and he/she will use such records
, documents and information only in a duly authorized manner in the interest of NRIBS. For the purpose of this clause \lquote Confidential Information\rquote  means information about NRIBS\rquote 
s business and that of its customers which is not available to the general public 
and which may be learnt by you in course of your employment. This includes but is not limited to information relating to the organization, its customer lists, employment policies, personnel and information about  NRIBS\rquote 
s products, process including ideas, concepts, projections, technology, manuals, drawing, designs, specifications, and all papers, resumes, records and other documents containing such Confidential Information.
\par 
\par 6.2   At no time, will the employee remove any Confidential Information from the office without the permission of NRIBS.
\par 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 6.3}{\fs21\insrsid12192131 \tab Breach of the conditions of this clause will render you liable to summary dismissal under clause 5 above in addition to any other remedy the NRIBS may have against you in law.
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 7. Solicitation of employees}{\fs21\insrsid12192131 .
\par The e
mployee agrees that for a period of twelve (12) months immediately following his/her termination from NRIBS or any reason, whether with or without causes, he/she shall not either directly or indirectly solicit, induce, recruit or encourage any of NRIBS
\rquote s employees to leave their employment, or take away employees of the NRIBS, either for himself/herself or for any other person or entity.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 8. Probationary Employment
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 8.1 The employee understands that the nature of employment of the employee shall be specified in Schedule 1 of this contract.
\par 
\par 8.2 Every employee entering into this Contract Employment shall be employed on probation unless specified otherwise in
\par Schedule 1 to the Contract herein.
\par 
\par 8.3 The probation period for an employee for the purposes of this Contract shall be extended to a period of six months unless provided for to the contrary in this Contract.
\par 
\par 8.4 The employee understands that during the period of probation a probationer employee shall only be entitled to those benefits as are detailed in Schedule I of this Contract.
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 8.5\tab 
At the outset, an employee during the subsistence of his/her probation period shall only be entitled to a limited number of paid leaves which shall be sough
t after seeking due permission from the concerned department of the NRIBS and the NRIBS reserves its right to either grant or reject such leaves as sought by the employee during his/her probation.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 8.6\tab Those employees who are classified as \'93CSR (Trainee)\'94 
by the NRIBS and are gathering on the job training shall not be entitled to either any paid leaves or any kind of benefits from the NRIBS.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 9. Notices
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 Notices may be given by you to the NRIBS at its registered office address. Notices may be given by the NRIBS to the employee at the address intimated by him/her in the official records.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 10. Applicability of the NRIBS Policy
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 The NRIBS shall be entitled to make policy declarations from time to time pertaining to matters like leave entitlement, maternity  leave, employees\rquote 
 benefits, working hours, transfer policy decisions of the NRIBS shall be binding on the employee and shall override this Agreement to that extent.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 11. Governing Law/Jurisdiction
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 The employee\rquote s employment with the NRIBS is subjected to Indian laws. All disputes shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the courts at New Delhi only.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 12. Acceptance of our offer
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 Please confirm your acceptance of this Contract of Employment signing and returning the duplicate copy for my attention within 14 days of 
receipt of this letter. We welcome you, and look forward to receiving your acceptance and to working with you.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Yours sincerely,
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Authorized Signatory
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par I accept the aforesaid terms and conditions of my employment. I have understood the implication thereof.
