\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\b\fs21\ul\insrsid9321002 SCHEDULE II
\par }{\fs21\ul\insrsid9321002 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 Specific Nature of the Employee\rquote s Duties:-
\par 
\par 1. Your duties involve interacting with clients and providing them with quality customer support.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid10502065 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 2. Major part of your job profile is to build excellent rapport with customer, an}{\fs21\insrsid10502065 swer their queries with }{
\fs21\insrsid9321002 efficiency and convert users into paid customers.}{\fs21\insrsid10502065 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 3. Customer retention & making sales will be the basis for performance
\par 4. Make and receive calls from overseas customers in US, UK & Canada, as applicable.
\par 5. Ensure internal and external customers satisfaction.
\par 6. Achieving the set targets.
\par 7. Would be handling outbound & inbound calls.
\par 8. Maintaining code of conduct and discipline.}{\fs21\ul\insrsid9321002   
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 SCHEDULE III
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\ul\insrsid9321002 GENERAL TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT
\par 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 Th
e following code of conduct shall be followed by all grades and levels.  The non-adherence of this code by an employee, being established after a preliminary enquiry by the Board of Directors, shall, in the interests of NRI Business Solutions Pvt. Ltd. (h
ereinafter referred to as \'93the company\'94
) lead to the termination of the said employee from the service of the company. Under such circumstances the said employee, shall be given an opportunity of being heard to present his/her explanations for the said act under scrutiny.
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin0\itap0\pararsid10502065 {\fs21\insrsid10502065\charrsid10502065 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\b\f1\fs21\insrsid9321002 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 1\tab}}\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent360 }\faauto\ls2\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 
Honesty}{\fs21\insrsid9321002 :
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\ilvl12\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 1.1\tab It shall be the duty of every employee to be honest towards his/her job profile to the extent envisaged under the said profile.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 2.   Equal Opportunity Employment:
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 2.1 The Company is an equal opportunity employer. Employment here is based solely upon one\rquote 
s individual merit and qualifications directly related to professional competence. The Company does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national 
origin, Ancestry, pregnancy status, sex, age, martial status, disability, medical condition or sexual orientation or any other basis protected by law.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 3. Harassment and Discriminate:
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 3.1 The Company is committed to maintaining the workplace environment free from discrimination
\par and harassment. In keeping with this policy, the company strictly prohibits unlawful discrimination
\par or harassment of any kind, including discrimination or harassment on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, age, mental or physical disability, medical condition, national origin, martial status or any other characteristics  protected by law.

\par 
\par 3.2 The Company strictly prohibits all form of unlawful harassment on the part old employee, temporary workers, independent contractors
, interns, and other professional service providers. The Company also prohibits unlawful harassment in any form, including verbal, physical or visual harassment.
\par 
\par 3.3 Complaints of sexual harassment sh
all be dealt with, in a very severe manner, which may also involve filing of a police complaint in the event of such matters being reported to the management. Sexual harassment means and includes, but is not limited to, making unwanted sexual advances and
 
request for sexual favors where (i) submission to such conduct is made an explicit or implicate term or condition of employment ;(ii) submission to or rejection of advances is used as the basis for employment decisions  or effect of substantially interfer
ing with an individual\rquote s work performance or creating  an intimidating, hostile or offensive working environment, even if it does not lead to tangible or economic job consequences.
\par 
\par 3.4\tab If you believe you\rquote ve been harassed by anyone with whom you come into c
ontact with at the Company, you must immediately report the incident to your supervisor, the director of Human Resources or both. Similarly, supervisors and managers who know of any such incident must immediately report the harassment to Human Resources w
h
ich will promptly and thoroughly investigate any complaints and take appropriate corrective action when it is warranted. Employees who are found to have violated this code are subject to disciplinary action (to be initiated by the Company) up to and inclu
ding immediate termination from the services of the company.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx180\tx720\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\ul\insrsid9321002 
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\rin720\lin720\itap0 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
3.5 Too often one hears stories of employees who were harassed, often for long period of time, but didn\rquote t feel comfortable coming forward. The Company hereby makes it entirely clear that it is n
ot, and never will be, the kind of Company in which any employee should ever feel that way. If one feels that there\rquote 
s a problem, please let your supervisor know about it right away so that any concern of discrimination or harassment can be investigated and addressed promptly and appropriately.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 4. Drug and Alcohol Use
\par }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 4.1 All and any forms of drugs, alcohol, tobacco, gutkha, paan, etc. are prohibited in the Company\rquote s work place. Only drugs for medicinal use accompanied by an appropriate prescription where a
nd when required shall be overlooked.
\par 
\par 4.2 The Company considers it to be incompatible with its employee\rquote s health and safety, not to mention their chances of long-term success with this company. Employees who are under the influence of alcohol or drugs whi
le on the job can endanger themselves and others, create serious disruptions. It is also made clear that the Company is not against the legal consumption of alcohol by adults. Example: Consumption of alcohol at a company sponsored event/party where the sa
me is served by the Company itself.
\par 
\par 4.3 The Company strictly prohibits the use, manufacture, possession, purchase, sale or distribution of any illegal drug or controlled substance while performing the Company business. It also goes without saying that whil
e performing Company business or attending a Company-sponsored event, alcohol  consumption is only allowed to the extent that it is situational, appropriate and its use does not lead to impaired performance or inappropriate behavior or endanger the safety
 of anyone or violet the law.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx0\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par 4.4 In cases where an employee\rquote s manager has reasonable suspicion to believe that the employee is under the influence of drugs and/or alcohol and such influence may adversely affect the employee\rquote s job performance safety or the
 safety of others in the workplace, the employee\rquote s manager may request an alcohol and/ or drug screening for the employee. A reasonable suspicion is based on objective symptoms such as factor relating to the employee\rquote 
s appearance, behavior, speech etc.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li720\ri396\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin396\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 4
.5 As a condition of employment, The Company requires each employee to abide by the term of this                                                                                                                                                               
 
                                                                                                       policy and notify if any criminal drug statute conviction for a violation occurring in the workplace within five days of such conviction. Each employee 
will be provided a copy of this policy and will be required to acknowledge that they have reviewed this policy.
\par }\pard \ql \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 4.6\tab Employees who violate the Company\rquote 
s substance abuse policy will be disciplined including potential termination and in certain situations, may be subjected to civil or criminal penalties.
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\rin720\lin720\itap0 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid9321002 5.   Weapons and workplace Violence}{\fs21\insrsid9321002 :
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 5.1\tab The Company\rquote s commitment to providing all its employees with a completely safe work environment extends to
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 any and all forms of weapons and workplace violence. The Company will not tolerate any level of violence, or the threat of violence\lquote 
s in its workplace. Under no circumstances should any employee bring any sort of weapon to work or threaten violence of any 
kind, and violations of this policy will result in appropriate disciplinary action, up to and including dismissal. As with other of this code, if any employee becomes aware of any violation of this policy, it shall be his /her duty to report the matter to
 the Human Resources department immediately.
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 {\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 6.   Disclosure of interests}{\fs21\insrsid4341762 :
\par 
\par 6.1 The employee shall consider it his/her responsibility to promptly disclose any interest he/she may have that could conflict with the interest of the Company. For Example; if one of the employee\rquote 
s family members (including parents, siblings or in laws) is become a Company supplier, customer, developer or competitor, that may not necessarily represent a conflict  of interest, but the right thing to do none the less is to let the 
supervisor/manager know about the situation immediately
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin0\itap0\pararsid4341762 {\fs21\insrsid4341762              }{\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762             
\par }\pard\plain \s4\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel3\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 7    Personal Investment
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs21\insrsid4341762 7.1 The employee will not invest, without prior approval from the company\rquote 
s Board of Directors, in a NRI customer, supplier, developer or competitor if it\rquote s at all likely that the employee\rquote s investment
\par could compromise the fulfillment of his/her responsibilities as the company\lquote s employee. As a general rule, greater the responsibilities at the company and the larger the amount of desired investment, It is more likely that he/sh
e is doing something that conflict (or could be perceived as conflicting ) with the Company\rquote  interests.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 8.   Gifts and Entertainment
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 8.1 Not all gifts }{\fs22\insrsid4341762 and entertainment necessarily represent conflict of interest; inexpensive \lquote token\'94 gifts, infrequent busi
ness meals and invitations to celebratory events can be consider ordinary aspects of many business relationships, provided that they aren\rquote 
t sufficiently excessive as to create the appearance of impropriety. Accepting an invitation to a cocktail party thrown by business partners for instance might be considered not only an acceptable business activity but a necessary}{\fs21\insrsid4341762 
 one for a sales employee.
\par 
\par }{\insrsid4341762 8.2 The employee should not, however accept any significant gift, payment or anything else of value from customers, 
vendors, consultants, or anyone else doing business with the Company, If the gift would likely be perceived as unduly influencing your business decision. Accepting a company T-shirt or coffee mug, for instance, isn\rquote t likely to change the employee
\rquote s assessment of a potential business relationship, but the}{\fs21\insrsid4341762 
\par same shall not be displayed in the company\rquote s workplace.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 9. Business Relationships}{\fs21\insrsid4341762 .
\par 9.1 Business relationships that one pursues outside one\rquote 
s work at the company requires above all- like many of the other situation described in this Code, your good faith and common sense as a rule, professional relationships with companies that compete with the Company are problematic for the Company; in part
icular, one should be extremely reluctant to accept personal employment or fees of any kind from any of the Company\rquote s suppliers, customers, developers or
\par competitors while one is employed here.
\par 
\par 
\par 9.2 It\rquote s also important to point out that business opportunities discovered through the employee\rquote 
s work at the Company belong first and foremost to the Company; the employee should not pursue such an opportunity unless he/she first seeks prior permission of the Company to pursue such interests.
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 10.  Friends and Relatives
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 
10.1 Similarly, business relationships with friends and relatives whose interests may conflict with the company can easily leave the employee with the sort of conflict of interest that can be difficult to happily resolve. Our rule here is simple: t
he employee should not enter into NRI Business Solutions-related business relationship with a close relative or significant other, including appointing them as an auditor, outside counsel or any other position that involves having financial dependence or 
influence on the Company, without first seeking permission from the Company.
\par 
\par 
\par 10.2 Senior executive sometimes get the opportunity to serve on other companies\rquote  boards. The Company is not against this as a matter of principle, but a few words of cautions are
 in order. For one, no employee should ever serve as a director/employee for a Company/legal entity that directly competes with the Company. In many cases it is fine to become a director of the Company\rquote 
s suppliers, customer or developers, but you should make sure you receive prior consent from the Company\rquote s Board of Directors.
\par 
\par 10.3 It is also understood that some of the employees will probably find themselves involved in personal relationships with people employed by one or more of the Company\rquote s competitor
s. In this case, as common sense applies: the employees should not, under any circumstances tell his/her significant other anything the company considers confidential, any more than a prudent person may reveal to a stranger.
\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid9321002 {\fs21\insrsid9321002 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 {\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 11. Confidential Company Information
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 11.1 The Company\rquote s \'93confidential information\'94 may include financial information, product information, user information, etc. The first rule is pretty simple: it is the employee\rquote 
s responsibility to exercise all due care to ensure that Company\rquote s co
nfidential material remains confidential. At times, however, some particular project or negotiation necessitates disclosing confidential information to a third party. Disclosure of confidential information should be on \'93a need to know \'93
basis. When such ins
tances arise, simply be sure to seek prior permission from the concerned Department of the Company so that an appropriate nondisclosure agreement can be drafted for the signature of all concerned parties. In addition, it shall be the duty of an employee t
o promptly report to the concerned Department of the Company any possible infringements of the Company\rquote s intellectual property. Every employee shall be personally responsible for reading the nondisclosure and other
\par allied agreements and abiding by its restrictions.
\par 
\par 11.2 There are, of course, \'93gray areas\'94 in which an employee\rquote s best judgment applies more fully than any hard-and fast rule.
\par 
\par \'93Suppose, for instance, that a friend who works at a non-profit charitable organization asks you for
\par advise about how to improve that site\rquote s search ranking? Using your Company knowledge to give your friend site-optimization tips that he or she could have found in any number of books, articles and websites isn\rquote 
t likely to seem problematic, but giving tips that aren\rquote t publicly known defiantly would be. As always your own judgment is likely to be your best yardstick but have to use that judgment.\rquote \rquote 
\par 
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel3\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 12 Trademarks, Logos and Copyrights
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs21\insrsid4341762 12.1 The name \'93NRI Business Solutions (P) Ltd.\'94
  and the names of numerous NRI BS products/services, and the various logos related to those products and services are all the Company\rquote s intellectual property, and unauthorized use of them can do real damage to the Company\rquote 
s public image. So it\rquote s important to remember that any use of the Company\rquote s logos, Trademark, services marks, etc. must be cleared in advance by the Company.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 13. The Company Partners
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 13.1 Just as an employee should be careful not to disclose Company\rquote s information, it\rquote s equally important 
not to disclose any confidential third party information with which the employee may be entrusted in the course of his/her work. The employee should take care not to accept any confidential information from third parties without first seeking prior permis
s
ion from the concerned Department of the Company, so that appropriate agreements can be drafted for the same. Also, please remember that you are personally responsible for reading the nondisclosure and other allied agreements and abiding by its restrictio
n.
\par 
\par 13.2 The employee should also be sure to obtain legal licenses for any third-party software you use in your work, and that you receive a publisher\rquote 
s consent, or consult the Legal Department, before copying any publication or software in connection with your work with the Company.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 14. Outside Communication
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 As a general rule, all the Company employees know that the Company believes in being extremely careful about disclosing the Company\rquote s information. It\rquote s almost always a bad idea to post discussion or i
nformation about the Company on the Internet or anywhere else unless you\rquote re authorized to do so as part of the employee\rquote 
s job. And the employee should never discuss the Company with member of the media unless he/she has been explicitly authorized to do so by the concerned Department of the Company.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s5\qj \li720\ri720\keepn\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel4\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 15 Business Transactions
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0\pararsid4341762 \f1\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs21\insrsid4341762 15.1 The employee\rquote 
s job at the Company may or may not involve significant record-keeping; but whenever appropriate, all the employees are responsible for helping to make sure that the Company\rquote 
s books are accurate. When an employee is involved in business transactions, he/she must ensure that the Company\rquote s procedures have been duly complied with.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 16. Reporting Irregularities
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 16.1 It shall be the duty of every employee to report to the concerned department of the Company, any irregularities that he/she may come across in the course of the Company\rquote s business.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 17. Private Policy
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 17.1 The following personal devices mentioned below are strictly prohibited at the Company\rquote s work place:
\par 
\par 1. Camera
\par 2. Camera Phones
\par 3. Any and all recordable device
\par 4. Any and all audio/visual/electronics equipment
\par 5. Any and all storage devices like floppy discs, compact discs, DVDs, zip drives, flash drives, etc.
\par 6. Laptops, PDAs, etc
\par 
\par 17.2 The devices above mentioned are not at all exhaustive in nature and may be amended from time to time in respect of technological advancements and/or changes.
\par 
\par 17.3 Any person found with any of the above-mentioned devices or any other devices, within t
he workplace of the Company, which in the view of the Company is likely to be detrimental to the interest of the Company shall be confiscated and appropriate proceedings for corporate espionage as per law shall be initiated.
\par 
\par 17.4 Employees of The Company are also strictly prohibited from accessing personal emails from any of the Company\rquote 
s computers. No work related document in any form shall be taken outside the Company Premises, without prior consent of the relevant supervisor/manager in writing.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid4341762 18. Saving
\par }{\fs21\insrsid4341762 18.1 The employees of the Company shall be bound by the terms and conditions of this Code.
\par 
\par 18.2 In the event of the Company deciding to amend the terms and conditions of this code or the employment contract, the employee understands and agrees that he/she will be accordingly bound by the amended terms and conditions of the amended code herein.

\par 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4341762 {\fs21\insrsid4341762 
\par }\pard \qj \li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin720\lin720\itap0 {\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par }{\fs21\insrsid12192131 
\par }}